Message-ID: <199703041632.KAA10459@dfw-ix7.ix.netcom.com>
Date: Tue, 04 Mar 1997 11:36:18 +0000
From: Thunderhawk Alpha <seafire@ix.netcom.com>
Subject: Successful (mostly) PCMCIA on RH4.1/axp

I installed the RH4.1 and althought there are still some problems related
(evidently) to named.init, I decided to try to get pcmcia working so that I
could use my pc-card modem. My config is UDB w/80Mb, Official RH4.1 with
updates installed from scratch.

First, the RH4.1/axp CD does not install the pcmcia stuff. IIRC, the pcmcia
is installed on the Intel side. <Hint: RedHat should do this on alpha as
well> In any event, I downloaded pcmcia-cs-2.8.23 from hyper.stanford.edu
(D.Hinds site). I went to do the make and it hiccupped on the smc and Xircom
ethernet card driver modules on what appeared to be duplicative includes of
functions or defines or something. Since I have neither card, I deleted
those two out of the makefile. All the rest went smoothly. I also tried to
download the pcmcia-cs-2.9.1 and compile but it puked at run time with an
undefined procedure 'Get_user'. I took this as a 2.1 kernel-ism and went
back to 2.8.23. So far, things are working properly, including being able to
ppp to Netcom via the pc-card modem (kudos to RedHat for the ppp auto-config
option as part of their network configuration - jabs for the fact that the
network config tool  bombs if you have a /etc/sysconfig/static-routes file....)

Since a couple of people have asked about this, I thought I'd let folks know...

