Message-ID: <199703121734.SAA06474@chiara.dei.unipd.it>
Date: Wed, 12 Mar 1997 18:07:21 +0000 (GMT)
From: Tim Waugh <tmw20@cam.ac.uk>
Subject: Haltiness

--- linux-2.1.29/arch/alpha/kernel/entry.S    Thu Mar  6 15:16:20 1997
+++ linux/arch/alpha/kernel/entry.S       Wed Mar 12 14:56:19 1997
@@ -622,7 +622,6 @@
         * We're called with $0 containing the address of
         * 'intr_count' and $1 containing 'intr_count+1'
         */
-       stl     $1,0($0)        /* intr_count = 1 */
        subq    $30,16,$30
        stq     $19,0($30)      /* save syscall nr */
        stq     $20,8($30)      /* and error indication (a3) */

Here's a fix for the "haltiness" problem that has been in since 2.1.27 or
so.

Thanks to Phil Blundell for that.

Tim.
