|>if I try to install it under 4.0 it tells me that it's for a different
|>architecture.  I'm running kernel 2.0.21 right now, and I'll be upgrading

This is a FAQ. This is because the arch identifier for Linux/Alpha changed
from axp to alpha sometime during the 2.2.x phase of RPM :) You can get
around this by upgrading to 2.3.x, or one of the later 2.2's, or you can
try installing it with the --ignorearch option.

