Subject: Re: AXPpci33 mboards
In-Reply-To: <Pine.OSF.3.91.970321133439.21196G-100000@caesar.iplink.net>

On Fri, 21 Mar 1997, Alvin Starr wrote:

> The above message started me to think(In general a dangerous thing). I 
> have a cople of 486s both 50 and 66Mhz and a P75. I alxo have a number of 
> Alphas. I sware that the Alphas are faster than the intel macines. I also 
> have to admit that the kernel compiles take a long time on the Alphas. So 
> I did a timing on the kernel compile.

Compiling for 64-bit RISC architecture is fundamentally slower than
compiling for 32-bit CISC architecture. RISC is far more dependent on
compiler optimizations. So benchmarking compilers is not an appropriate test
of a machine's speed.

Mike Epstein - mjepst@hcs.harvard.edu - http://hcs.harvard.edu/~mjepst/

